+/*
+ * Without an SDL window (-display vnc, none, egl-headless, dbus, gtk, or sdl,gl=on; the same choice
+ * as the Glide device's, hw/3dfx/fxdisp.c) the guest's GL renders offscreen instead of into a GLX
+ * context on the SDL window: a desktop OpenGL context on an EGL display that needs no window
+ * system (Mesa's surfaceless platform: a GPU's render node or llvmpipe; else the first EGL device,
+ * else the default display), current on an EGL pbuffer the size of the guest's display. The
+ * pbuffer is the "window": the guest's framebuffer 0, GL_BACK and its default viewport are the
+ * pbuffer's, so no GL call needs rewriting. At every wglSwapBuffers the frame is read
+ * (glReadPixels of framebuffer 0, which also resolves a multisampled pbuffer) and handed to
+ * fxdisp, which shows it in the first graphic console (VNC, screendump) in place of the VGA while
+ * the context's 3D output is active (MGLActivateHandler), with the guest's gamma ramp
+ * (wglSetDeviceGammaRamp3DFX) applied. The VGA comes back when the guest deactivates its window or
+ * the GL context ends.
+ *
+ * libEGL.so.1 is opened at run time, so the binary links nothing new; when it, the display or a
+ * context can't be had, the guest's wglChoosePixelFormat/wglCreateContext fail and QEMU keeps
+ * running. mglcntx_linux.c hands its MGL* entry points over here while MGLEglActive(); the
+ * SDL/GLX path is unchanged. The WGL constants and tables below repeat mglcntx_linux.c's, whose
+ * copies are private to it.
